    "answer": {
      "short": "He omitted $1$ inside the brackets: $2x^3+6x^2+2x=2x(x^2+3x+1)$.",
      "worked": "The highest common factor is $2x$. Each term must contribute a term inside the brackets; the final $2x$ contributes $1$.\n$$2x^3+6x^2+2x=2x(x^2+3x+1).$$",
